  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 242 AM MDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nNot expecting impactful weather today but will see continuing\nwarming trend as upper level ridge moves over Idaho by late\nmorning into afternoon. No precipitation expected today with a\ncontinued warming trend and high temperatures in the 70s \nvalleys and 60s and 70s higher elevations as closer to normal \nreadings return. Ridge moves east Tuesday with southerly flow \naloft returning which will increase the moisture content and \nwill have the main precipitation event for the week most likely \nTuesday into Wednesday. This will likely not be a significant \nrain producer with the highest QPF in the southern and eastern \nmountains along with the highest probability. Only slight \nchances to chances elsewhere. Beyond Tuesday will have mainly \ndry and warm conditions Wednesday through next Monday with above\nnormal temperatures expected with many low elevations into the \n80s both Thursday and Friday. An upper level trof passing to \nnorth Friday may bring breezy to windy conditions.",
